{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added explicit `uniform(0, 100)` priors for `sigma_a` and `sigma_y`. These parameters already had finite bounds `<lower=0, upper=100>` and no explicit prior, so the added statements make the implicit bounded-uniform prior explicit for SafeStan's unique-prior requirement without changing the posterior apart from a parameter-independent normalizing constant. No data changes were required.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> J;
  int<lower=0> N;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> county;
  vector[N] u;
  vector[N] x;
  vector[N] x_mean;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  vector[3] b;
  vector[J] eta;
  real mu_a;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_a;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_y;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[J] a;
  vector[N] y_hat;

  a = mu_a + sigma_a * eta;

  for (i in 1 : N) {
    y_hat[i] = a[county[i]] + u[i] * b[1] + x[i] * b[2] + x_mean[i] * b[3];
  }
}
model {
  mu_a ~ normal(0, 1);
  eta ~ normal(0, 1);
  b ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_a ~ uniform(0, 100);
  sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 100);
  y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":1,"N":1,"county":[1],"u":[4.483415604746555],"x":[5.636727131862694],"x_mean":[6.693977123906681],"y":[1.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
